e simple engineered features\n    \n    # Product of key numeric features\n    numeric_features = ['carbon', 'hardness', 'strength', 'thick', 'width', 'len']\n    numeric_features = [f for f in numeric_features if f in X_train.columns]\n    \n    if len(numeric_features) >= 2:\n        # Create some interaction terms\n        X_train['carbon_hardness'] = X_train['carbon'] * X_train['hardness']\n        X_test['carbon_hardness'] = X_test['carbon'] * X_test['hardness']\n    \n    # Log transformation of skewed features (if applicable)\n    if 'strength' in X_train.columns:\n        # Check if strength has significant skewness\n        X_train['log_strength'] = np.log1p(X_train['strength'])\n        X_test['log_strength'] = np.log1p(X_test['strength'])\n    \n    return X_train, X_test\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790972882102},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the evaluation results and the task requirements, I have successfully optimized the pipeline for the anneal dataset. Here's my final solution:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've achieved the best CV score of **0.02943** (compared to the baseline of 0.03063) using 12 evaluations out of the 64-budget limit.\n\n## Key Improvements Implemented\n\n1. **Proper Categorical Encoding**: Used LabelEncoder to convert categorical variables to numeric format, which is essential for the TabPFN model to work effectively.\n\n2. **Domain-Specific Feature Engineering**:\n   - Created interaction feature: carbon × hardness (physically relevant relationship in steel processing)\n   - Added log transformation of strength feature to reduce skewness\n\n3. **Robust Data Preprocessing**:\n   - Proper handling of missing values by filling with 'missing' category\n   - Ensured consistency between training an